        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9179561f-9966-50e4-9923-245db9d92d34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Connell, Robert Connell, Berthold Viertel, Paul Muni, Richard Thorpe, Gladys Lehman\n- Works: Seven Faces, A Friend of Napoleon, The Saturday Evening Post, The Most Dangerous Game, The Hounds of Zaroff, Collier's, Bloodlust!, Thrill of a Romance\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" was published in the June 30, 1923, issue of The Saturday Evening Post.\n- Richard Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff,\" was first published in Collier's on January 19, 1924.\n- Richard Connell's best known work \"The Most Dangerous Game\" was filmed three years after the 1923 publication of \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- The film Seven Faces was based on Richard Connell's \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- Berthold Viertel directed Seven Faces.\n- Paul Muni starred in Seven Faces in his second screen appearance.\n- Bloodlust! is a 1961 American horror thriller film based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"\n- Thrill of a Romance was directed by Richard Thorpe and written by Richard Connell and Gladys Lehman.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f92ef93c-cf2a-50dc-bd83-35b92eb827b0",
        "text": "Page: Seven Faces. Sentence: Based upon the piece of short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" which was published in the June 30, 1923, issue of \"The Saturday Evening Post\" magazine by popular writer Richard Connell (whose best known work, \"The Most Dangerous Game\", was filmed three years later), it was directed by Berthold Viertel and stars Paul Muni in his second screen appearance.\nPage: The Most Dangerous Game. Sentence: \"The Most Dangerous Game\", also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff\", is a short story by Richard Connell, first published in \"Collier's\" on January 19, 1924.\nPage: Bloodlust!. Sentence: is a 1961 American horror thriller film based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"\nPage: Thrill of a Romance. Sentence: The film was directed by Richard Thorpe and written by Richard Connell and Gladys Lehman.",
